<title>UK: GM, Renault British venture to create 900 jobs.</title>
<headline>GM, Renault British venture to create 900 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp. and France's Renault announced plans Thursday to build a new medium-sized van line at a plant in Luton, north of London, creating 900 jobs.</p>
<p>The 180 million pound ($300.9 million) investment will also safeguard 1,800 existing jobs at the IBC Vehicles plant.</p>
<p>Both groups are keen to boost their presence in what is an expanding marketplace, industry analysts said, noting that manufacturers are not concerned about the dilution of their strong brand names in light commercial vehicles because styling is not so individual in the sector.</p>
<p>The western European market for light commercial vehicles, which includes pick-ups and small trucks, is put at 1.3 million sales per year -- or one-tenth of the car market. The growth rate is 6 percent annually.</p>
</text>
